[E0437] Error: cannot return a `Mapped<Forwards<i64>, i64>` that borrows `step`
    ╭─[ err/542_a_chain_borrows_what_its_closure_reads/main.wip:11:12 ]
    │
 10 │     val step = 3
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── `step` declared here
 11 │     return xs.forwards().map((x) => x + step)
    │            ─────────────────┬────────────────
    │                             ╰────────────────── `step` is a local of `leaves`, dropped when it returns
    │
    │ Help: answer a value that owns its data, as a `String` owns its bytes
    │
    │ Note: a view that leaves a function may only borrow what its reference parameters refer to
────╯
[E0436] Error: `shifted` is used after `step`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/542_a_chain_borrows_what_its_closure_reads/main.wip:23:17 ]
    │
 21 │     var shifted = xs.forwards().map((x) => x + step)
    │         ───┬───
    │            ╰───── `shifted` borrows `step`
 22 │     step = 20
    │     ──┬─
    │       ╰─── `step` assigned here
 23 │     val first = shifted.next()
    │                 ───┬───
    │                    ╰───── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `shifted` before `step` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
    │
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
────╯
